WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.030
Hello, hello, hello, and welcome

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.050
to English Learning for Curious

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.940
Minds, by Leonardo English, the show

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.770
where you can listen to fascinating

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:17.209
stories and learn weird and wonderful

00:00:17.219 --> 00:00:19.209
things about the world at the same

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.089
time as improving your English.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.820
I'm Alastair Budge, and today we are

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.590
continuing our three-part mini-series

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.200
on stories from North Korea.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.250
In part one, we talked about Otto

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.539
Warmbier, the American student

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.640
who travelled to North Korea as a

00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:40.690
tourist and returned home in a coma.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.269
In part three, we’ll be talking about

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.980
Kim Jong-il’s unusual passion for cinema.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.900
But in today's episode, part two,

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.619
we are going to talk about one of

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.419
the most extraordinary and brazen

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.540
political assassinations of the

00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:00.239
twenty-first century: the murder of

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.470
Kim Jong-nam, the half-brother of North

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.130
Korea's Supreme Leader, Kim Jong-un.

00:01:06.681 --> 00:01:09.361
It's a story involving a weapon of

00:01:09.371 --> 00:01:12.491
mass destruction, a fake reality TV

00:01:12.491 --> 00:01:15.381
show, two young women who had no idea

00:01:15.421 --> 00:01:17.161
they were committing a crime, and

00:01:17.161 --> 00:01:20.131
a plan almost certainly approved by

00:01:20.131 --> 00:01:22.621
the murdered man’s brother himself.

00:01:23.221 --> 00:01:25.291
So, let's not waste a minute

00:01:25.581 --> 00:01:27.331
and get right into it.

00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:32.171
Very few people expect to be murdered.

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:34.941
Even fewer people expect

00:01:35.031 --> 00:01:36.691
to be murdered in public.

00:01:37.191 --> 00:01:40.291
And, I would imagine at least, even fewer

00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:43.731
people expect to be murdered in public by

00:01:43.781 --> 00:01:46.471
two young women they’ve never met before.

00:01:47.231 --> 00:01:50.111
But not everyone is the older

00:01:50.111 --> 00:01:52.601
brother of the leader of North Korea.

00:01:53.681 --> 00:01:56.191
Still, from what we know about the

00:01:56.191 --> 00:01:58.991
events of the morning of the 13th of

00:01:59.001 --> 00:02:04.411
February, 2017, Kim Jong-nam expected

00:02:04.411 --> 00:02:07.181
it to be a day like any other.

00:02:08.391 --> 00:02:11.931
He had arrived alone at terminal 2 of

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:14.271
Kuala Lumpur International Airport.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.401
It was busy, as usual.

00:02:16.871 --> 00:02:19.891
Noisy, slightly chaotic, full of

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:22.291
people dragging wheelie suitcases

00:02:22.481 --> 00:02:24.841
and staring at departure boards.

00:02:26.071 --> 00:02:29.071
The 45-year-old Kim looked perfectly

00:02:29.091 --> 00:02:33.011
ordinary: short, shaved hair, slightly

00:02:33.041 --> 00:02:35.741
overweight, a light grey suit, a

00:02:35.741 --> 00:02:38.641
small, dark rucksack over his shoulder.

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:41.851
He makes his way towards

00:02:41.891 --> 00:02:43.651
the self check-in kiosks.

00:02:44.071 --> 00:02:46.961
In a few hours he will be on the plane to

00:02:46.981 --> 00:02:49.851
Macau, in south-east China, where he has

00:02:49.851 --> 00:02:52.121
been living quietly for several years.

00:02:53.211 --> 00:02:55.311
His name, on his diplomatic

00:02:55.311 --> 00:02:57.815
passport at least, is Kim Chol.

00:02:58.823 --> 00:03:02.371
But of course this is not his real name.

00:03:03.271 --> 00:03:05.801
His real name is Kim Jong-nam.

00:03:06.471 --> 00:03:07.921
He is forty-five years old.

00:03:08.351 --> 00:03:10.311
He is the eldest son of the

00:03:10.311 --> 00:03:12.361
late North Korean leader Kim

00:03:12.361 --> 00:03:14.961
Jong-il, and the half-brother of

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.271
its current leader, Kim Jong-un.

00:03:18.221 --> 00:03:20.781
And in a matter of minutes,

00:03:21.241 --> 00:03:23.671
Kim Jong-nam will be dead.

00:03:25.028 --> 00:03:27.308
At approximately nine o'clock

00:03:27.318 --> 00:03:29.468
in the morning, a young woman

00:03:29.738 --> 00:03:31.778
approaches him from behind.

00:03:32.818 --> 00:03:34.638
Before he has the chance to

00:03:34.638 --> 00:03:36.938
react, she wipes something on

00:03:36.938 --> 00:03:38.968
his face with her bare hand.

00:03:39.948 --> 00:03:41.358
She then turns around

00:03:41.638 --> 00:03:43.178
and walks away quickly.

00:03:44.108 --> 00:03:47.028
Moments later, a second woman approaches

00:03:47.328 --> 00:03:49.908
and does the same thing, pressing her

00:03:49.928 --> 00:03:52.978
palm against his eyes and his cheeks.

00:03:53.988 --> 00:03:57.728
She too disappears quickly into the crowd.

00:03:58.678 --> 00:04:01.288
The whole thing takes seconds.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.678
Nobody around them appears

00:04:03.678 --> 00:04:05.428
to notice anything unusual.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:10.078
After all, it wasn’t particularly violent.

00:04:10.518 --> 00:04:14.448
Weird and unexpected, yes, but nobody

00:04:14.448 --> 00:04:17.298
was shot or stabbed; it was like

00:04:17.518 --> 00:04:20.238
it was all some elaborate prank,

00:04:20.388 --> 00:04:22.948
a joke for a hidden camera show.

00:04:24.168 --> 00:04:25.878
But it quickly becomes

00:04:25.878 --> 00:04:28.458
clear that this is no joke.

00:04:29.378 --> 00:04:32.388
Kim Jong-nam feels it immediately.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.938
He walks to a nearby airport

00:04:34.948 --> 00:04:37.538
information desk and tells the staff

00:04:37.788 --> 00:04:39.548
that someone has sprayed something in

00:04:39.548 --> 00:04:42.128
his face, that his eyes are burning,

00:04:42.498 --> 00:04:45.231
and that he is feeling deeply unwell.

00:04:46.428 --> 00:04:49.138
There’s CCTV footage of this

00:04:49.168 --> 00:04:51.178
entire thing; you can see him

00:04:51.228 --> 00:04:52.888
gesturing to the airport staff.

00:04:53.288 --> 00:04:55.080
“Help! I need a doctor”.

00:04:56.388 --> 00:04:58.818
He is taken to the airport clinic.

00:04:59.578 --> 00:05:00.948
Within minutes, he is

00:05:00.948 --> 00:05:02.438
deteriorating rapidly.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.518
He goes into convulsions.

00:05:04.818 --> 00:05:06.108
He can barely breathe.

00:05:06.938 --> 00:05:10.178
An ambulance is called, but by the time

00:05:10.178 --> 00:05:12.728
it arrives, it is already too late.

00:05:13.378 --> 00:05:15.748
He dies on the way to hospital.

00:05:16.758 --> 00:05:19.348
The time from the attack to his

00:05:19.348 --> 00:05:22.068
death is less than twenty minutes.

00:05:23.118 --> 00:05:26.498
Now, to understand why Kim Jong-nam

00:05:26.778 --> 00:05:29.368
was murdered, and why his brother

00:05:29.788 --> 00:05:31.938
almost certainly ordered it, we

00:05:31.938 --> 00:05:33.408
need to go back to the beginning.

00:05:33.878 --> 00:05:36.628
To the strange and privileged and

00:05:36.638 --> 00:05:39.718
ultimately cursed life of the man who was

00:05:39.718 --> 00:05:43.158
born to rule North Korea, but whose fate

00:05:43.158 --> 00:05:45.968
was to be murdered in a Malaysian airport.

00:05:46.818 --> 00:05:49.398
Kim Jong-nam was born on the 10th

00:05:49.518 --> 00:05:53.428
of May, 1971, the oldest son of

00:05:53.428 --> 00:05:56.358
the then leader-to-be, Kim Jong-il.

00:05:57.278 --> 00:05:59.898
Now, as a quick reminder of some

00:05:59.898 --> 00:06:02.388
North Korean history, North Korea

00:06:02.631 --> 00:06:04.818
has been run by the same family

00:06:05.078 --> 00:06:07.888
since its founding in 1948.

00:06:08.638 --> 00:06:11.678
Kim Il-sung was the first leader, ruling

00:06:11.688 --> 00:06:15.168
until his death in 1994, when power passed

00:06:15.168 --> 00:06:17.978
to his son, Kim Jong-il, who we'll be

00:06:17.978 --> 00:06:20.298
hearing more about in the next episode.

00:06:21.258 --> 00:06:24.198
And when Kim Jong-il died, in

00:06:24.218 --> 00:06:28.628
2011, power should have gone to

00:06:28.628 --> 00:06:30.778
his oldest son, Kim Jong-nam.

00:06:31.538 --> 00:06:32.948
But it didn’t.

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:36.808
Now, we’ll get to why in a moment, but

00:06:36.888 --> 00:06:40.188
first, to the early life of Kim Jong-nam.

00:06:41.188 --> 00:06:43.228
His mother was a woman named

00:06:43.238 --> 00:06:44.988
Song Hye-rim, who was a

00:06:45.008 --> 00:06:47.388
glamorous and well-known actress.

00:06:47.848 --> 00:06:50.848
She was also married to another man,

00:06:51.118 --> 00:06:54.398
and was reportedly forced to divorce him

00:06:54.618 --> 00:06:56.838
before becoming Kim Jong-il’s mistress.

00:06:57.438 --> 00:07:00.871
And importantly, the pair never married,

00:07:00.871 --> 00:07:03.748
and Kim kept their relationship, and

00:07:04.018 --> 00:07:06.578
the existence of their son, secret

00:07:06.718 --> 00:07:08.848
from his father for many years.

00:07:09.618 --> 00:07:13.188
Clearly, this led to a slightly odd early

00:07:13.188 --> 00:07:15.948
existence for the young Kim Jong-nam.

00:07:16.548 --> 00:07:18.178
He did not go to school.

00:07:18.518 --> 00:07:21.578
He was educated at home by his aunt,

00:07:21.838 --> 00:07:23.998
and his only childhood playmate,

00:07:24.278 --> 00:07:26.738
for several years, was his cousin.

00:07:28.178 --> 00:07:30.568
As he grew older, however, his

00:07:30.568 --> 00:07:32.458
father started to acknowledge him

00:07:32.638 --> 00:07:35.208
and began to invest in his future.

00:07:36.128 --> 00:07:38.598
Kim was sent abroad for school,

00:07:38.798 --> 00:07:40.698
to Geneva, in Switzerland.

00:07:41.318 --> 00:07:44.498
He returned to Pyongyang in 1988

00:07:44.758 --> 00:07:47.058
and was given government roles,

00:07:47.298 --> 00:07:49.018
eventually becoming head of

00:07:49.018 --> 00:07:50.828
North Korea's Computer Committee.

00:07:51.678 --> 00:07:53.738
He was being groomed, so it

00:07:53.738 --> 00:07:56.168
seemed, to be the next in line.

00:07:57.378 --> 00:07:59.898
He was also regarded, by the

00:07:59.898 --> 00:08:01.808
standards of the Kim family at

00:08:01.808 --> 00:08:04.328
least, as something of a reformer.

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:08.648
He was cosmopolitan, worldly, interested

00:08:08.858 --> 00:08:11.308
in technology and the outside world.

00:08:12.087 --> 00:08:14.468
But he would also be described as

00:08:14.798 --> 00:08:18.048
sensitive, hot-tempered, and he had

00:08:18.048 --> 00:08:20.218
a weakness for a few things that

00:08:20.218 --> 00:08:22.798
weren’t exactly legal in North Korea.

00:08:23.808 --> 00:08:25.928
He was known to enjoy the casinos of

00:08:25.928 --> 00:08:28.778
Macau and the freedoms that came with

00:08:28.778 --> 00:08:30.978
living outside the hermit kingdom.

00:08:31.918 --> 00:08:34.348
He was, to use his own choice of

00:08:34.348 --> 00:08:37.168
words, a "totally capitalist kid."

00:08:38.258 --> 00:08:39.778
Unfortunately, it would be

00:08:39.828 --> 00:08:41.978
capitalism that would bring him down.

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:45.488
Specifically, the allure of Mickey

00:08:45.488 --> 00:08:48.568
Mouse and large flasks of Coca Cola.

00:08:49.708 --> 00:08:54.128
In May 2001, he tried to go to Japan.

00:08:55.418 --> 00:08:57.708
He managed to get to Tokyo airport,

00:08:57.918 --> 00:09:00.588
but Japanese officials smelled

00:09:00.598 --> 00:09:03.048
something fishy about his passport.

00:09:04.588 --> 00:09:07.378
It was, supposedly, a Dominican

00:09:07.388 --> 00:09:10.294
Republic passport with the name “Pang

00:09:10.294 --> 00:09:12.978
xiong”, which translates, somewhat

00:09:13.058 --> 00:09:16.538
unfortunately, as "Fat Bear" in Chinese.

00:09:17.438 --> 00:09:19.908
When his true identity was revealed,

00:09:20.168 --> 00:09:22.868
and he was asked why he was trying

00:09:22.868 --> 00:09:25.328
to enter Japan on a fake passport,

00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:28.008
he famously told the officials that

00:09:28.008 --> 00:09:30.938
he wanted to visit Tokyo Disneyland.

00:09:31.838 --> 00:09:34.838
This was hugely embarrassing to

00:09:34.838 --> 00:09:37.028
North Korea, and to his father.

00:09:37.688 --> 00:09:40.098
The son of the North Korean leader,

00:09:40.268 --> 00:09:43.018
the heir apparent to one of the last

00:09:43.258 --> 00:09:45.448
officially communist regimes on Earth,

00:09:45.958 --> 00:09:48.878
had been caught red-handed travelling on

00:09:48.878 --> 00:09:52.278
a forged passport to go to a theme park.

00:09:52.848 --> 00:09:55.358
To Disneyland, nonetheless, the

00:09:55.358 --> 00:09:57.708
Mecca of American capitalism.

00:09:58.928 --> 00:10:02.108
His father was said to be furious.

00:10:02.668 --> 00:10:05.608
All public engagements for this young

00:10:05.658 --> 00:10:07.918
Disneyland-lover were cancelled.

00:10:08.958 --> 00:10:11.638
And that, essentially, was the end

00:10:11.768 --> 00:10:14.168
of Kim Jong-nam's political career.

00:10:15.068 --> 00:10:17.658
He moved into a kind of comfortable

00:10:17.688 --> 00:10:20.188
but permanent exile, drifting

00:10:20.188 --> 00:10:22.378
around China, but based mainly

00:10:22.378 --> 00:10:24.738
in the gambling centre of Macau.

00:10:25.638 --> 00:10:27.908
His younger half-brother, Kim

00:10:27.908 --> 00:10:30.578
Jong-un, became the heir apparent.

00:10:31.438 --> 00:10:34.178
And when Kim Jong-il died in

00:10:34.178 --> 00:10:37.708
December 2011, it was Kim Jong-un

00:10:38.058 --> 00:10:40.978
who took power, not Kim Jong-nam.

00:10:41.838 --> 00:10:44.548
Now, if you have brothers or sisters,

00:10:44.928 --> 00:10:46.568
you know that the relationship

00:10:46.748 --> 00:10:49.088
can sometimes be intense.

00:10:49.648 --> 00:10:52.518
And, you might think, this relationship

00:10:52.568 --> 00:10:55.078
would only be further intensified

00:10:55.358 --> 00:10:57.118
if you think that one of you will

00:10:57.118 --> 00:10:59.128
become the supreme leader of the

00:10:59.128 --> 00:11:01.298
world's most reclusive dictatorship.

00:11:02.028 --> 00:11:04.888
But the funny thing is that Kim

00:11:04.888 --> 00:11:08.418
Jong-un and Kim Jong-nam had no

00:11:08.458 --> 00:11:11.638
relationship; they never actually met.

00:11:12.328 --> 00:11:14.468
They were kept completely separate

00:11:14.648 --> 00:11:16.758
as children, so it’s not like

00:11:16.788 --> 00:11:19.398
Kim Jong-un held some huge grudge

00:11:19.408 --> 00:11:21.358
against his brother for something

00:11:21.368 --> 00:11:23.318
he did when they were teenagers, and

00:11:23.508 --> 00:11:25.408
finally decided to get his revenge.

00:11:26.208 --> 00:11:29.028
It wasn’t revenge, as far as we know it.

00:11:29.538 --> 00:11:32.858
This 2017 airport murder

00:11:33.288 --> 00:11:34.978
was purely business.

00:11:36.228 --> 00:11:38.478
For the relatively new Supreme

00:11:38.488 --> 00:11:41.008
Leader, Kim Jong-un, his older

00:11:41.018 --> 00:11:43.048
half-brother was a problem.

00:11:43.918 --> 00:11:45.438
He wasn’t an immediate,

00:11:45.958 --> 00:11:47.208
operational problem.

00:11:47.558 --> 00:11:50.638
Kim Jong-nam had no obvious power base

00:11:50.638 --> 00:11:53.768
in Pyongyang, no army, no political

00:11:53.768 --> 00:11:55.658
faction he could call his own.

00:11:56.078 --> 00:11:58.288
He wasn’t particularly charismatic,

00:11:58.528 --> 00:12:00.928
and didn’t seem to have any grand

00:12:00.928 --> 00:12:03.158
designs on overthrowing his brother.

00:12:04.028 --> 00:12:06.168
But he was still alive.

00:12:06.528 --> 00:12:08.178
He was still the eldest

00:12:08.178 --> 00:12:09.818
son of Kim Jong-il.

00:12:10.658 --> 00:12:13.598
And that made him, in theory, a

00:12:13.668 --> 00:12:16.508
potential rallying point for anyone

00:12:16.728 --> 00:12:18.748
who might want an alternative.

00:12:19.858 --> 00:12:22.148
There were whispers that China was

00:12:22.148 --> 00:12:24.618
quietly keeping Kim Jong-nam as

00:12:24.618 --> 00:12:27.538
what one analyst called "a spare", a

00:12:27.538 --> 00:12:30.648
sort of insurance policy in case Kim

00:12:30.648 --> 00:12:33.098
Jong-un ever needed to be replaced.

00:12:34.088 --> 00:12:36.278
That was not a comfortable

00:12:36.288 --> 00:12:37.968
thought for Kim Jong-un.

00:12:38.998 --> 00:12:41.578
And he had already shown, more

00:12:41.578 --> 00:12:43.658
than once, that he was willing to

00:12:43.688 --> 00:12:46.388
eliminate those he perceived as rivals.

00:12:47.188 --> 00:12:49.068
His uncle and former mentor,

00:12:49.238 --> 00:12:51.508
a man named Jang Song-thaek,

00:12:51.838 --> 00:12:54.771
had been executed in 2013.

00:12:55.348 --> 00:12:57.078
The message to any

00:12:57.168 --> 00:12:59.298
potential rival was clear.

00:13:00.628 --> 00:13:02.968
And there had, in fact, been

00:13:02.968 --> 00:13:04.918
multiple assassination attempts

00:13:05.078 --> 00:13:07.618
on Kim Jong-nam over the years.

00:13:08.558 --> 00:13:12.708
One reported attempt in Budapest in 2006.

00:13:12.778 --> 00:13:15.051
Another in 2012.

00:13:15.738 --> 00:13:19.178
Kim Jong-nam was well-aware of the threat.

00:13:19.868 --> 00:13:21.428
He had written to his half-brother

00:13:21.741 --> 00:13:24.988
in 2012, according to South Korean

00:13:24.988 --> 00:13:27.238
reports, begging for his life.

00:13:27.828 --> 00:13:30.048
He knew he was not safe.

00:13:31.018 --> 00:13:34.088
So, perhaps, he was one of those few

00:13:34.088 --> 00:13:36.488
people who does wake up and think

00:13:36.708 --> 00:13:39.228
there is a not insignificant chance

00:13:39.438 --> 00:13:41.778
that this day might be his last.

00:13:42.828 --> 00:13:46.758
And in fact, there is some evidence to

00:13:46.758 --> 00:13:50.038
suggest that he wasn’t merely a portly

00:13:50.368 --> 00:13:53.948
North Korean gambler; there is credible

00:13:53.948 --> 00:13:56.578
evidence that Kim Jong-nam had been

00:13:56.578 --> 00:13:59.848
working as an informant for the CIA.

00:14:00.538 --> 00:14:02.738
He had been meeting with American

00:14:02.748 --> 00:14:04.718
intelligence agents, usually

00:14:04.718 --> 00:14:06.798
in Singapore and Malaysia.

00:14:07.418 --> 00:14:09.558
Security footage from his final

00:14:09.558 --> 00:14:12.128
trip reportedly showed him in a

00:14:12.138 --> 00:14:14.978
hotel lift with a man identified

00:14:15.188 --> 00:14:17.158
as an American intelligence agent.

00:14:18.028 --> 00:14:20.208
And his backpack, which was

00:14:20.368 --> 00:14:22.968
found after the attack, contained

00:14:23.228 --> 00:14:26.638
some 120,000 dollars in cash.

00:14:28.218 --> 00:14:31.438
Whether his potential CIA connections

00:14:31.598 --> 00:14:33.568
had anything to do with the timing

00:14:33.578 --> 00:14:35.988
of the assassination, we cannot say.

00:14:36.698 --> 00:14:39.678
But what we do know is that North Korean

00:14:39.698 --> 00:14:41.768
intelligence had been tracking his

00:14:41.768 --> 00:14:44.668
movements, and on that Monday morning

00:14:44.668 --> 00:14:46.988
in February, their plan was ready.

00:14:47.978 --> 00:14:50.408
So, to the murder itself.

00:14:51.388 --> 00:14:54.238
The weapon used to kill Kim Jong-nam

00:14:54.558 --> 00:14:58.108
was something called “VX nerve agent”.

00:14:59.168 --> 00:15:01.698
It is classified by the United Nations

00:15:01.908 --> 00:15:04.118
as a weapon of mass destruction,

00:15:04.588 --> 00:15:07.138
and is the most toxic of all

00:15:07.178 --> 00:15:09.268
known chemical warfare agents.

00:15:10.178 --> 00:15:12.518
It looks and feels a little like

00:15:12.548 --> 00:15:15.338
motor oil: it’s sort of oily,

00:15:15.748 --> 00:15:18.888
colourless, odourless, and tasteless.

00:15:19.478 --> 00:15:22.828
It looks harmless enough, but as little as

00:15:22.828 --> 00:15:26.528
a single drop on the skin can be lethal.

00:15:27.638 --> 00:15:29.958
It attacks your nervous system,

00:15:30.328 --> 00:15:32.728
and kills within minutes.

00:15:33.408 --> 00:15:36.638
15 minutes, in the case of Kim Jong-nam.

00:15:37.958 --> 00:15:40.478
And, just in case you were worried that

00:15:40.478 --> 00:15:42.008
you might get your cake measurements

00:15:42.018 --> 00:15:44.708
wrong and accidentally concoct a bit of

00:15:44.718 --> 00:15:47.988
VX nerve agent at home, no, it’s something

00:15:47.988 --> 00:15:50.188
that requires incredibly sophisticated

00:15:50.218 --> 00:15:52.688
equipment and expertise to make.

00:15:53.428 --> 00:15:55.748
Only a handful of countries in the world

00:15:56.038 --> 00:15:58.068
are believed to have the capability to

00:15:58.068 --> 00:16:01.008
produce it: the United States, Russia,

00:16:01.548 --> 00:16:04.098
Syria, and, of course, North Korea.

00:16:05.258 --> 00:16:08.518
Now, another perhaps unbelievable

00:16:08.528 --> 00:16:10.778
part of this story is that the two

00:16:10.788 --> 00:16:13.538
women that administered this nerve

00:16:13.538 --> 00:16:15.738
agent, the two young women who

00:16:15.788 --> 00:16:18.308
killed Kim Jong-nam, they weren’t

00:16:18.358 --> 00:16:20.678
highly trained North Korean agents.

00:16:21.858 --> 00:16:25.303
The younger one was called Siti Aisyah.

00:16:25.588 --> 00:16:28.188
She was a twenty-five year old Indonesian.

00:16:28.788 --> 00:16:31.628
And the other was a 29-year-old

00:16:31.628 --> 00:16:34.578
Vietnamese woman called Doan Thi Huong.

00:16:36.048 --> 00:16:38.878
Their story, which emerged after

00:16:38.878 --> 00:16:40.688
their arrest in the days following

00:16:40.688 --> 00:16:44.028
the murder, went like this: they

00:16:44.028 --> 00:16:46.498
had each been approached separately,

00:16:46.708 --> 00:16:49.218
in the weeks beforehand, by men

00:16:49.418 --> 00:16:51.898
they understood to be scouts for

00:16:51.898 --> 00:16:54.038
a Japanese entertainment company.

00:16:55.138 --> 00:16:57.518
They were offered money, around a

00:16:57.518 --> 00:16:59.818
hundred dollars each, to take part

00:17:00.028 --> 00:17:02.828
in a prank “hidden camera” TV show.

00:17:03.898 --> 00:17:06.448
The premise was simple: they would

00:17:06.458 --> 00:17:09.448
approach strangers in public places and

00:17:09.448 --> 00:17:12.328
wipe a harmless liquid on their faces.

00:17:13.448 --> 00:17:15.948
Hidden cameras would capture the reaction.

00:17:16.348 --> 00:17:18.008
It was all for entertainment.

00:17:19.355 --> 00:17:21.925
They had each done the prank multiple

00:17:21.925 --> 00:17:24.935
times, in shopping malls and at the

00:17:24.935 --> 00:17:27.695
airport itself, with different targets,

00:17:27.975 --> 00:17:30.345
using what they were told was baby

00:17:30.345 --> 00:17:33.415
oil or a similar harmless substance.

00:17:34.125 --> 00:17:34.915
They were filmed.

00:17:35.265 --> 00:17:36.815
The footage was shown back to them.

00:17:37.375 --> 00:17:39.165
It was a bit of harmless fun.

00:17:40.385 --> 00:17:43.095
Everything seemed above board.

00:17:44.475 --> 00:17:46.555
On the morning of the 13th of

00:17:46.565 --> 00:17:48.585
February, they were each given a

00:17:48.595 --> 00:17:51.235
liquid to apply to their hands.

00:17:52.035 --> 00:17:54.005
They were told who they should

00:17:54.005 --> 00:17:56.365
approach: that portly looking

00:17:56.365 --> 00:17:58.275
fellow with the black rucksack.

00:17:59.735 --> 00:18:01.995
They approached their target separately,

00:18:02.535 --> 00:18:06.005
each carrying what was, in effect, one

00:18:06.005 --> 00:18:08.815
component of a binary chemical weapon.

00:18:09.795 --> 00:18:13.345
The VX was only created at the moment

00:18:13.405 --> 00:18:16.325
of contact, when the two substances

00:18:16.545 --> 00:18:18.985
combined on Kim Jong-nam's face.

00:18:20.335 --> 00:18:24.465
This design was deliberate and ingenious.

00:18:25.025 --> 00:18:27.085
It meant the women themselves were

00:18:27.085 --> 00:18:29.225
not exposed to a lethal dose of

00:18:29.245 --> 00:18:31.815
VX, because neither of them was

00:18:31.815 --> 00:18:33.885
carrying the fully formed agent.

00:18:34.805 --> 00:18:37.385
It also gave them genuine,

00:18:37.685 --> 00:18:39.245
believable ignorance.

00:18:39.935 --> 00:18:41.805
They really did think, or

00:18:42.015 --> 00:18:43.465
could convincingly claim to

00:18:43.465 --> 00:18:45.575
think, that it was a prank.

00:18:46.315 --> 00:18:48.205
After all, they had done it before,

00:18:48.615 --> 00:18:51.215
many times, with no consequences.

00:18:52.605 --> 00:18:54.685
After the attack, both women

00:18:54.795 --> 00:18:56.665
went quickly to wash their hands,

00:18:56.785 --> 00:18:58.325
as they had been instructed.

00:18:59.155 --> 00:19:01.065
Then they went about their day.

00:19:02.395 --> 00:19:05.005
Doan Thi Huong later went back to

00:19:05.005 --> 00:19:06.485
look for the rest of the film crew,

00:19:06.925 --> 00:19:09.735
and, finding no one, headed home.

00:19:10.555 --> 00:19:11.735
She was arrested at the

00:19:11.735 --> 00:19:13.615
airport two days later.

00:19:14.955 --> 00:19:17.705
The men who had recruited them, the

00:19:17.925 --> 00:19:20.455
North Korean handlers, had slipped

00:19:20.515 --> 00:19:22.905
through passport control and boarded

00:19:22.905 --> 00:19:25.305
flights out of Malaysia within hours

00:19:25.305 --> 00:19:27.675
of the attack, long before police

00:19:27.905 --> 00:19:29.845
even knew what they were dealing with.

00:19:30.475 --> 00:19:32.365
They were back in Pyongyang by

00:19:32.365 --> 00:19:34.335
the time the newspapers reported

00:19:34.335 --> 00:19:36.045
that Kim Jong-nam was dead.

00:19:37.415 --> 00:19:39.515
And what followed was a

00:19:39.515 --> 00:19:42.025
serious diplomatic crisis.

00:19:42.985 --> 00:19:45.575
The North Korean ambassador to Malaysia

00:19:45.935 --> 00:19:48.715
called a press conference and accused

00:19:48.735 --> 00:19:51.765
Malaysian authorities of conspiring

00:19:51.775 --> 00:19:54.305
with "hostile forces" to falsely

00:19:54.335 --> 00:19:56.585
implicate North Korea in the killing.

00:19:57.275 --> 00:20:00.385
He demanded that the body be handed over

00:20:00.385 --> 00:20:02.935
to the North Korean embassy immediately.

00:20:03.725 --> 00:20:05.365
Malaysia refused.

00:20:05.975 --> 00:20:08.430
A North Korean diplomat and a staff

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.855
member from Air Koryo, North Korea's

00:20:10.855 --> 00:20:13.535
state airline, were named as suspects.

00:20:14.155 --> 00:20:16.305
They took refuge inside the

00:20:16.305 --> 00:20:18.195
North Korean embassy in Kuala

00:20:18.195 --> 00:20:20.835
Lumpur, and refused to come out.

00:20:21.855 --> 00:20:24.505
The body remained in a Kuala Lumpur

00:20:24.745 --> 00:20:27.255
hospital mortuary, and became

00:20:27.255 --> 00:20:29.405
the subject of an increasingly

00:20:29.415 --> 00:20:31.505
surreal diplomatic standoff.

00:20:32.405 --> 00:20:34.445
Malaysian authorities needed

00:20:34.445 --> 00:20:36.895
DNA to formally identify the

00:20:36.895 --> 00:20:38.895
victim; he had been travelling,

00:20:39.275 --> 00:20:42.022
remember, under the name Kim Chol.

00:20:42.725 --> 00:20:46.085
So what they needed was a DNA sample

00:20:46.235 --> 00:20:48.435
from one of Kim’s family members.

00:20:49.285 --> 00:20:52.065
Of course, his half-brother, Kim Jong-un

00:20:52.445 --> 00:20:54.775
wasn’t exactly going to volunteer himself.

00:20:55.565 --> 00:20:59.165
But eventually, DNA from Kim Jong-nam's

00:20:59.165 --> 00:21:01.395
son, who was living in Macau,

00:21:01.855 --> 00:21:04.195
confirmed the dead man’s identity.

00:21:05.385 --> 00:21:07.765
Malaysia then announced the results

00:21:07.925 --> 00:21:10.895
of a forensic examination: VX

00:21:10.932 --> 00:21:13.175
nerve agent had been found on

00:21:13.175 --> 00:21:15.725
Kim Jong-nam's face and eyes.

00:21:17.135 --> 00:21:20.225
This was extraordinary not only because

00:21:20.225 --> 00:21:22.075
of what it confirmed about how he

00:21:22.075 --> 00:21:24.395
had been killed, but because of what

00:21:24.415 --> 00:21:27.265
it implied about who had killed him.

00:21:28.085 --> 00:21:31.795
Manufacturing VX requires state resources.

00:21:32.415 --> 00:21:34.655
Only a government could have done this.

00:21:35.475 --> 00:21:37.765
The United States, Russia, and

00:21:37.765 --> 00:21:40.415
Syria had no reason to do it.

00:21:41.265 --> 00:21:43.595
North Korea, or to be precise,

00:21:43.785 --> 00:21:45.765
the supreme leader of North Korea,

00:21:46.045 --> 00:21:47.885
had a pretty serious reason.

00:21:49.495 --> 00:21:52.365
And what followed was a peculiar

00:21:52.375 --> 00:21:54.265
hostage situation, of sorts.

00:21:54.935 --> 00:21:57.125
North Korea announced that it would

00:21:57.125 --> 00:21:59.305
not allow nine Malaysian citizens

00:21:59.545 --> 00:22:02.265
currently in Pyongyang to leave North

00:22:02.265 --> 00:22:05.475
Korea until Malaysia handed over Kim

00:22:05.475 --> 00:22:07.905
Jong-nam's body and released the North

00:22:07.905 --> 00:22:09.985
Koreans sheltering in the embassy.

00:22:10.935 --> 00:22:13.995
Malaysia, in turn, declared that it

00:22:13.995 --> 00:22:15.525
would not allow the North Koreans

00:22:15.525 --> 00:22:17.435
in the embassy to leave until the

00:22:17.475 --> 00:22:19.275
Malaysian citizens were freed.

00:22:20.375 --> 00:22:22.985
After several weeks of increasingly

00:22:23.075 --> 00:22:26.065
tense negotiations, a deal was reached.

00:22:26.565 --> 00:22:28.315
The Malaysians came home.

00:22:28.755 --> 00:22:29.755
The North Koreans in the

00:22:29.775 --> 00:22:31.795
embassy were allowed to leave.

00:22:32.625 --> 00:22:35.025
Kim Jong-nam's body was eventually

00:22:35.185 --> 00:22:36.985
handed over to North Korea.

00:22:38.455 --> 00:22:40.715
The four North Korean suspects who

00:22:40.715 --> 00:22:42.415
had fled the country on the morning

00:22:42.415 --> 00:22:44.585
of the murder were never charged.

00:22:45.275 --> 00:22:47.065
They remain in North Korea

00:22:47.225 --> 00:22:49.345
to this day, beyond the reach

00:22:49.455 --> 00:22:51.095
of any international court.

00:22:52.125 --> 00:22:54.865
Malaysia and North Korea severed

00:22:54.885 --> 00:22:57.065
diplomatic relations entirely.

00:22:57.795 --> 00:23:00.125
The two countries, which had maintained

00:23:00.455 --> 00:23:03.655
unusually warm ties for decades, had

00:23:03.665 --> 00:23:05.875
no further official relationship.

00:23:07.095 --> 00:23:10.645
And as for Siti Aisyah and Doan Thi Huong,

00:23:10.875 --> 00:23:13.285
the two young women who had delivered the

00:23:13.295 --> 00:23:15.875
poison, they were charged with murder.

00:23:16.915 --> 00:23:18.625
If they were convicted,

00:23:18.955 --> 00:23:20.965
they faced death by hanging.

00:23:22.585 --> 00:23:24.855
When their trial began, it

00:23:24.855 --> 00:23:26.725
raised some serious questions

00:23:27.005 --> 00:23:29.545
about guilt and manipulation.

00:23:30.305 --> 00:23:32.605
The defence argued, that

00:23:32.605 --> 00:23:34.005
they had been deceived.

00:23:34.305 --> 00:23:35.225
They were used.

00:23:35.405 --> 00:23:37.195
They didn’t know what they were carrying.

00:23:37.385 --> 00:23:38.765
They had not known they

00:23:38.765 --> 00:23:39.655
were killing anyone.

00:23:40.185 --> 00:23:42.525
They were not assassins; they were

00:23:42.535 --> 00:23:45.775
victims, tools that the North Korean state

00:23:45.945 --> 00:23:49.405
had picked up and used and then discarded.

00:23:50.705 --> 00:23:53.185
The prosecution argued that it

00:23:53.185 --> 00:23:55.055
did not matter whether they knew.

00:23:55.625 --> 00:23:57.755
They had carried out the act.

00:23:58.185 --> 00:23:59.815
They were responsible.

00:24:01.045 --> 00:24:02.955
A couple of years afterwards, and

00:24:03.225 --> 00:24:05.315
having been awaiting trial since the

00:24:05.315 --> 00:24:07.775
day of the murder, all charges were

00:24:07.775 --> 00:24:10.585
dropped, and the women were released.

00:24:11.705 --> 00:24:14.105
No one has ever been convicted

00:24:14.325 --> 00:24:16.715
of the murder of Kim Jong-nam.

00:24:17.685 --> 00:24:19.395
Now, there is one more

00:24:19.395 --> 00:24:20.645
layer to this story.

00:24:21.885 --> 00:24:24.085
Among Kim Jong-nam's possessions when he

00:24:24.095 --> 00:24:26.815
died was something that tells you a great

00:24:26.815 --> 00:24:29.385
deal about the life he had been living,

00:24:29.745 --> 00:24:32.155
and the threat he'd been living under.

00:24:33.285 --> 00:24:37.045
In his backpack, alongside the 120,000

00:24:37.055 --> 00:24:39.525
dollars in cash, there were twelve

00:24:39.585 --> 00:24:42.455
vials of something called atropine.

00:24:43.815 --> 00:24:46.235
Atropine is the antidote

00:24:46.535 --> 00:24:48.485
to VX nerve agent.

00:24:49.905 --> 00:24:53.355
Kim Jong-nam had, in other words, been

00:24:53.355 --> 00:24:56.305
carrying the specific antidote to the

00:24:56.315 --> 00:24:59.465
specific weapon that was used to kill him.

00:25:00.205 --> 00:25:02.325
He knew he was a target.

00:25:02.675 --> 00:25:04.475
He knew what would most

00:25:04.495 --> 00:25:06.065
probably be used to kill him.

00:25:06.405 --> 00:25:09.075
He had the means to survive it, if

00:25:09.105 --> 00:25:11.825
only he'd been able to use it in time.

00:25:12.685 --> 00:25:15.145
But the attack was so fast,

00:25:15.185 --> 00:25:17.385
and so expertly executed,

00:25:17.725 --> 00:25:19.665
that he never had the chance.

00:25:20.655 --> 00:25:23.015
So, to wrap up, what

00:25:23.055 --> 00:25:24.445
do we make of all this?

00:25:25.515 --> 00:25:28.585
The assassination of Kim Jong-nam was not

00:25:28.645 --> 00:25:31.955
a crime of passion, or brotherly rivalry.

00:25:32.425 --> 00:25:34.825
It was a meticulously planned state

00:25:34.885 --> 00:25:37.195
operation, years in the making,

00:25:37.635 --> 00:25:39.975
carried out with a weapon of mass

00:25:39.975 --> 00:25:42.565
destruction, and designed so that

00:25:42.575 --> 00:25:45.085
the only people who ever faced any

00:25:45.085 --> 00:25:47.565
consequences were two young women

00:25:47.825 --> 00:25:49.275
who didn't know what they were doing.

00:25:50.335 --> 00:25:53.185
The four men who actually planned and

00:25:53.225 --> 00:25:55.695
executed it went home to Pyongyang.

00:25:56.645 --> 00:25:59.055
No court has ever heard the full

00:25:59.065 --> 00:26:01.365
story of what happened that morning.

00:26:02.935 --> 00:26:05.185
And what it tells us about Kim

00:26:05.185 --> 00:26:08.805
Jong-un is simple, if chilling.

00:26:09.465 --> 00:26:11.475
He has eliminated his uncle,

00:26:11.765 --> 00:26:13.695
his half-brother, and countless

00:26:13.725 --> 00:26:15.625
others who posed even a

00:26:15.635 --> 00:26:18.045
theoretical threat to his rule.

00:26:18.955 --> 00:26:21.635
The message is clear: there is no

00:26:21.635 --> 00:26:24.445
such thing as a safe distance from

00:26:24.445 --> 00:26:26.935
Kim Jong-un, and there is no such

00:26:26.935 --> 00:26:29.565
thing as a safe member of his family.

00:26:30.795 --> 00:26:34.195
Kim Jong-nam, so it seems, knew this.

00:26:34.685 --> 00:26:36.385
He carried the antidote.

00:26:36.675 --> 00:26:39.125
He just never got the chance to use it.

00:26:41.005 --> 00:26:43.665
OK, then, that is it for today's episode

00:26:43.875 --> 00:26:46.295
on the assassination of Kim Jong-nam.

00:26:46.615 --> 00:26:47.995
I hope it's been an interesting one,

00:26:48.235 --> 00:26:49.835
and that you've learnt something new.

00:26:50.495 --> 00:26:52.725
As a reminder, this is part two

00:26:52.915 --> 00:26:54.915
of our three-part mini-series

00:26:55.085 --> 00:26:56.965
on stories from North Korea.

00:26:57.265 --> 00:26:58.675
In part one, we talked

00:26:58.685 --> 00:26:59.835
about Otto Warmbier.

00:27:00.155 --> 00:27:02.345
And in part three, coming up next,

00:27:02.445 --> 00:27:04.505
we'll be talking about a very different

00:27:04.575 --> 00:27:07.095
kind of North Korean story: Kim

00:27:07.095 --> 00:27:09.365
Jong-il's extraordinary obsession with

00:27:09.375 --> 00:27:12.035
cinema, and the filmmaker and actress

00:27:12.125 --> 00:27:14.545
he kidnapped to make movies for him.

00:27:15.525 --> 00:27:17.325
You've been listening to English Learning

00:27:17.325 --> 00:27:19.895
for Curious Minds by Leonardo English.

00:27:20.275 --> 00:27:22.955
I'm Alastair Budge, you stay safe, and

00:27:22.955 --> 00:27:25.115
I'll catch you in the next episode.

